. * HYPOTHESIS TEST FOR H2 * (Please adapt according to your needs)
. 
.         * Please add a verbal description of your model here
.         
.         
.         *This regression model investigates whether having a daughter (has_da
> ughter) is associated with their political ideology (left). It controls for t
> he total number of children (nb_kid), age (age), and age squared (age2) to ac
> count for non-linear age effects. Socio-economic controls include current lif
> e satisfaction (plh0182) and household income (hghinc). The model also includ
> es dummies for family status (pgfamstd), education level (pgpsbil), employmen
> t status (pgemplst), survey year (syear), sex (sex), federal state (sampreg),
>  and migration background (migback). The analysis is limited to individuals o
> lder than 15 (if age > 15), and standard errors are clustered by individual I
> D (cluster(pid)) to account for repeated observations over time. Robust stand
> ard errors are used to correct for heteroskedasticity.
. 
.         * As an example, and for illustrative purposes we consider a linear O
> LS regression
.         
.         
.          reg left has_daughter nb_kid age age2  plh0182 hghinc i.(pgfamstd pg
> psbil pgemplst syear sex sampreg migback) if age>15, cluster(pid) robu

